# bookings — empty env templates (mirrors the `env:` list in module.manifest).
# The generator appends these (blank) to the project's .env.example section; set
# real values in .env and NEVER commit them.
#
# OPTIONAL — you normally do NOT need to set anything here:
#   BOOKINGS_API_URL  Where the booking API lives. Resolution order in the
#                     frontend client is BOOKINGS_API_URL -> BACKEND_URL.
#                       * fullstack  : leave BLANK — the frontend already reaches
#                                      the backend at http://<name>-api:8080 via
#                                      BACKEND_URL (set by the base). Works as-is.
#                       * dotnet-api : nothing to set — the API IS this service.
#                       * nextjs-app : the UI has no backend of its own. Point this
#                                      at a deployed bookings .NET API AND pass it
#                                      into the web container by adding
#                                        BOOKINGS_API_URL: ${BOOKINGS_API_URL:-}
#                                      to the environment in
#                                        services/<name>/<name>.compose.yml
#                                      (see the module README, "nextjs-app
#                                      integration"). Until then the booking UI
#                                      renders but shows no services (graceful).
#
# Not a secret, but kept in .env so it stays out of committed files.
BOOKINGS_API_URL=
#
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Backend-only knob (NOT in the env: contract list, because bookings ships no
# compose fragment to inject it — set it directly on the .NET service if needed):
#   BOOKINGS_SEED=false   Disable the first-run sample data. By default the .NET
#                         backend seeds a couple of example services + upcoming
#                         slots ONLY when the bookings tables are empty (a brand-new
#                         install), so the booking flow works end-to-end out of the
#                         box. Add `BOOKINGS_SEED: "false"` to the backend service's
#                         environment (or just delete the sample rows) to turn it
#                         off. It never overwrites existing data.
